{"result":[{"biographic_references":[],"contributors":{"authors":[{"aliases":[],"checked":"0","codes":["devos.matthew"],"name":"DeVos, Matt"},{"aliases":[],"checked":"0","codes":["ebrahimi.javad-b"],"name":"Ebrahimi, Javad"},{"aliases":[],"checked":"1","codes":["ghebleh.mohammad"],"name":"Ghebleh, Mohammad"},{"aliases":[],"checked":"0","codes":["goddyn.luis-a"],"name":"Goddyn, Luis"},{"aliases":[],"checked":"1","codes":["mohar.bojan"],"name":"Mohar, Bojan"},{"aliases":[],"checked":"1","codes":["naserasr.reza"],"name":"Naserasr, Reza"}],"author_references":[],"editors":[]},"database":"Zbl","datestamp":"2008-05-22T13:48:22Z","document_type":{"code":"j","description":"journal article"},"editorial_contributions":[{"language":"English","reviewer":{"author_code":null,"reviewer_id":null,"name":null,"sign":null},"text":"Summary: The unit distance graph \\(\\mathcal{R}\\) is the graph with vertex set \\(\\mathbb{R}^2\\) in which two vertices (points in the plane) are adjacent if and only if they are at Euclidean distance 1. We prove that the circular chromatic number of \\(\\mathcal{R}\\) is at least 4, thus improving the known lower bound of \\(32/9\\) obtained from the fractional chromatic number of \\(\\mathcal{R}\\).","contribution_type":"summary"}],"id":5277979,"identifier":"1140.05303","keywords":[],"language":{"languages":["English"],"addition":[null]},"license":[],"links":[{"identifier":"10.1137/060664276","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/060664276"}],"msc":[{"code":"05C15","scheme":"msc2020","text":"Coloring of graphs and hypergraphs"},{"code":"05C10","scheme":"msc2020","text":"Planar graphs; geometric and topological aspects of graph theory"},{"code":"05C62","scheme":"msc2020","text":"Graph representations (geometric and intersection representations, etc.)"}],"references":[],"source":{"book":[],"pages":"461-465","series":[{"acronym":null,"issn":[{"number":"0895-4801","type":"print"},{"number":"1095-7146","type":"electronic"}],"issue":"2","issue_id":21927